# How the claim transaction finally reached Chipnet
#
# The engine's broadcast path (via the Electrum servers' own node) rejected the
# identical transaction as non-BIP68-final from tip 337146 to 337173 while the
# covenant coin was confirmed at height 337144 (merkle proof verified against
# the header at 337144). The same bytes were submitted directly to both servers
# at tip 337174 and accepted. Captured output:
#
#  chipnet.imaginary.cash tip 337174 ACCEPTED bf9fa85020c9396405c75e781b481ab05eb8e2fe015a2ce604254a0d99899dc3
#  chipnet.bch.ninja      tip 337174 ACCEPTED bf9fa85020c9396405c75e781b481ab05eb8e2fe015a2ce604254a0d99899dc3
#
# The inline script used for that submission is now in the repository as
# scripts/broadcast-raw.ts. Re-submitting the same bytes after confirmation
# (tip 337180) correctly reports:
#
#  chipnet.imaginary.cash tip 337180 REJECTED the transaction was rejected by network rules. transaction already in block chain
#  chipnet.bch.ninja      tip 337180 REJECTED the transaction was rejected by network rules. transaction already in block chain
#
# The claim confirmed in block 337175: 1 input (p2sh, 58,500 sat) ->
# 1 output (p2pkh, 57,000 sat to bchtest:qr5wd0g0ql3tzwyztdedlfe2x7xdtp520yvtvvwmxe),
# 348 bytes, fee 1,500 sat, version 2, nSequence 3, no signature.
